From 5b95b1bb3e6aa9b589b417f376cd0992902abd6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mjbommar <michael.bommarito@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 22:02:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH bpf-next 2/2] bpf, x86: use instruction_pointer helpers in
 ex_handler_bpf
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ex_handler_bpf accesses the trapped PC via regs->ip directly
(once to report the arena violation, once to skip past the
faulting instruction). The kernel already exposes
instruction_pointer() and instruction_pointer_set() as the
arch-generic accessors for exactly this pt_regs field (see
arch/x86/include/asm/ptrace.h:285-294), and they compile to
the same trivial code on x86 as the direct field access.

Convert both call sites to use the helpers. No functional
change on x86 — the helpers are static-always-inline wrappers
around regs->ip. Matches the pattern used by kprobes, uprobes,
and ftrace throughout the tree, where direct pt_regs field
accesses have been migrated to the generic helpers over time.

Before:
    bpf_prog_report_arena_violation(is_write, addr, regs->ip);
    regs->ip += insn_len;
After:
    bpf_prog_report_arena_violation(is_write, addr, instruction_pointer(regs));
    instruction_pointer_set(regs, instruction_pointer(regs) + insn_len);

Generated code identical on x86 defconfig; bpf_jit_comp.o byte-
for-byte size unchanged (verified with make ARCH=x86_64 defconfig
+ BPF_JIT=y).

Signed-off-by: mjbommar <michael.bommarito@gmail.com>

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c b/arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c
index 28e6041ea145..8a217fd3a006 100644
--- a/arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c
+++ b/arch/x86/net/bpf_jit_comp.c
@@ -1491,13 +1491,13 @@ bool ex_handler_bpf(const struct exception_table_entry *x, struct pt_regs *regs)
 		arena_reg = FIELD_GET(FIXUP_ARENA_REG_MASK, x->fixup);
 		off = FIELD_GET(DATA_ARENA_OFFSET_MASK, x->data);
 		addr = *(unsigned long *)((void *)regs + arena_reg) + off;
-		bpf_prog_report_arena_violation(is_write, addr, regs->ip);
+		bpf_prog_report_arena_violation(is_write, addr, instruction_pointer(regs));
 	}
 
 	/* jump over faulting load and clear dest register */
 	if (reg != DONT_CLEAR)
 		*(unsigned long *)((void *)regs + reg) = 0;
-	regs->ip += insn_len;
+	instruction_pointer_set(regs, instruction_pointer(regs) + insn_len);
 
 	return true;
 }
-- 
